   * Retrieve a specific product image from the frozen snapshot captured at the time an order was placed.
   *
   * When a customer places an order, every product image visible at that moment is preserved as an immutable snapshot image record. This endpoint retrieves a single snapshot image by its unique identifier, scoped within a specific order item's product snapshot.
   *
   * The returned image includes the frozen URL and display order as they existed at purchase time, providing an authoritative historical record even if the seller later changes, reorders, or deletes the original product images. This supports accurate order history display and dispute resolution by showing exactly what the product listing looked like when the customer made the purchase.
